  "client_view_text": " A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked over to investigate, his boots sinking into the damp sand.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and pulled out A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked over to investigate, his boots sinking into the wet sand.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and pulled out a piece of paper, yellowed with age. Unfurling it, he saw that it was a letter, written in elegant script.\n\n\"Dear whoever finds this,\" the letter began, \"I am writing to you from the ship, 'Maverick's Revenge.' We set sail from England in 1850, bound for the New World. But fate had other plans. We were caught in a storm and wrecked on these very shores. I am the only survivor, and I have been stranded here for...I dare not think how long. I have seen the beauty of this place, but also its cruelty. I"
}